says 'So much depends on me, but ever since the influence of this Church of Self began to be a problem, more and more of my Underquarry crew have failed to follow my orders! Being assigned to the Underquarry is the highest of honors a Dwarf or even a Gnome could ever hope to achieve! Why would one risk losing the favor of Brell by abandoning one's sacred duties? Yet that is precisely what has happened. I, and these few who remain here, are all that are left who remain dedicated in service to Brell. Yet it is strange, Brell no longer appears, or has not been seen or heard from in a very long time. I may need your [help] if we are to restore the Underquarry to its proper functioning.'\nYou say, 'How could I help?'\nClontik Beardburner says 'Much to do, much to do. Your help would genuinely be appreciated. I will need help with restoring order in the [Stonequarry] as well as in the [Metal Mines]. When you have completed these tasks I have [other work] I need completed.'\nYou say, 'What about the Stonequarry?'\nClontik Beardburner says 'I do not know how long I've been here - eons, it seems - and always the Underquarry has performed flawlessly. Then the miserable Emissaries came. I can't tell you how much I loathe them, for they have turned most of my mining crew against me, against the Way of Brell, and spread chaos to the Underquarry. It is MY responsibility that this sacred place runs as it's supposed to, MY name that will be tarnished in the eyes of Brell! If my subordinates can't be trusted to do their duty, then they have become the enemies of all Underfoot. Please, go to the Stonequarry room, and [eliminate] these disloyal engineers and foremen.'\nYou say, 'I'll eliminate them'\nClontik Beardburner says 'Thank you, friend. Go at once, into the room to the east, then take the southwest tunnel to get to the first Stonequarry room.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Chaos in the Stonequarry'.\nGo to the main Stonequarry chamber and eliminate the disobedient engineers and foremen.\nClontik said his subordinates in the first Stonequarry room must be dealt with first; go there and begin searching for the engineers and foremen.\n\n---\n\nExplore Southern Stonequarry 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nKill 5 Stonequarry Engineer 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nKill 5 Stonequarry Foreman 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nSpeak with Clontik 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nYou say, 'Hail, Clontik Beardburner'\nClontik Beardburner looks at you wearily. \"I wish it hadn't been necessary to destroy the rebels, but there is no other way, it seems. Brell's Way must prevail. Brell's absence has been felt, and until He returns those who hinder His will must be dealt with severely.\"\n_Reward:_\nExperience",
