enkar Everhot'\nTenkar Everhot says 'Goodwill to ya. I trust you're not just another apeling from the surface, here to make mischief along with the other creatures that have [invaded] my beloved Underquarry?'\nYou say, 'They invaded?'\nTenkar Everhot says 'Aye, and we need an army to hold them off, an army we haven't got! Some of these other dwarves and gnomes are ready to start wringing their hands, but not me. I'll be fighting them off with my axe and hammer, till there's no more air in me lungs! Long centuries have I served Brell Serilis, and wherever he may have gone, I'll not give up an inch of his realm as long as I've sworn to protect it! But, I have to admit, [disaster] looms!'\nYou say, 'A disaster?'\nTenkar Everhot says 'We have only a limited amount of time for talking! We've got [duties] that must be done!'\nYou say, 'What duties?'\nTenkar Everhot says 'Take your pick. First, our negotiations with the Bellikos have broken down. We now suffer Lady Envy of the Bellikos pushing into the Underquarry with a clockwork army. I suppose we'll need to put a [mission] together to blast them out. If that was too tame for ya, maybe you could get together fifty or so adventurers and lead a [raid] into that first stone quarry of ours, something big has broken its way out of the lower mines and won't be restrained.'\nYou say, 'Let's hear about that mission'\nTenkar Everhot says 'The situation is dire, she'll be here any minute, I can almost smell her! If she completes her armored subordinate clockwork, her army will be indestructible, and the Underquarry will be hers. That must not happen! Will you [accept] the mission to drive her off?'\nYou say, 'I accept'\n_Without pre-requisites:_\nTenkar Everhot says 'Look, I don't mean ta be rude, but I just don't trust ya. Go talk to that fool Clontik Beardburner. If you can convince him that you're not just some overgrown monkey, then maybe you'll be able to help me.'\n_With pre-requisites:_\nTenkar Everhot says 'We have no reserves left to maintain order in the Underquarry, and we certainly can't afford to contend with another faction of belligerent squatters! I can hear Lady Envy coming with her clockwork armies. We don't have nearly enough dwarves or gnomes to stop them! Seek her out and see if you can work out an accomodation somehow, but the Underquarry must remain under the control of Brell Serilis, though he is not here to hear our pleas! If she remains unreasonable, look for something you can use against her, and resolve things the hard way, destorying the clockworks one at a time until she gives up. Tell me when your ready to [go].'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Scent of a Woman'.\nLady Envy has brought an army of clockworks into the Underquarry to fulfill her twisted megalomania. Clontik and the other dwarved and gnomes loyal to Brell Serilis will have no choice but to submit to her unless you can successfully intervene.\nYou say, 'I wish to go'\nTenkar Everhot says 'Find your way to Lady Envy; see if she will reveal a weakness somehow.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered The Underquarry - Scent of a Woman.\n\n---\n\nConfront Lady Envy regarding her plans for the Underquarry 0/1 (The Underquarry)\n_Lady Envy is found in the room due east from the zone-in. There are a few KOS mobs you'll have to clear before you speak with her (including a see-invis genati)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Lady Envy'\nLady Envy says 'Well for you and these Dwarves and Gnomes, there shall be NO accommodation, NO mercy. We Bellikos came and explained very, very carefully the tenets of self respect, of free will, but always we have been met with the most unfortunate stubbornness from them. The time for consideration has passed. As soon as I complete repairs to my Subordinate, my armored army will crush them! Which reminds me, I must find only \\*exact\\* matches for the missing parts or he might just think for himself.'\nYour task 'Scent of a Woman' has been updated.\n_After hailing Lady Envy, the eight \"Destroy\" steps listed below open up. The \"Loot\" steps open up after the killing of individual named clockworks._\nDestroy at least five of the Tantalum clockworks 0/5 (The Underquarry)\nDestroy Ptoleus, the Tantalum clockwork coordinator 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nLoot a Counterrotating Flywheel Piston from Ptoleus 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nDestroy five of Lady Envy's Therium clockworks 0/5 (The Underquarry)\nDestroy Trathon, the Therium clockwork coordinator 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nLoot a Difference Machine Gearbox from Trathon 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nDestroy five of Lady Envy's Periluminum clockworks 0/5 (The Underquarry)\nDestroy Aurdred, the Periluminum clockwork coordinator 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nLoot a Servogizmonic Manipulator from Aurdred 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nDestroy at least five of the Galvanite clockworks 0/5 (The Underquarry)\nDestroy Gracho, the Galvanite clockwork coordinator 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nLoot a Pellucinite Cylinder from Gracho 0/1 (The Underquarry)\n_The Therium and Periluminum clockwork groups are located in the eastern caves/tunnels. (Location for periluminums: -50, -1035, -208)_\n_The Tantalum and Galvantie groups are located in the south/southwest caves/tunnels. Locations for map file:_\nP 144.4714, 596.5150, -262.8911, 0, 0, 0, 1, Ptoleus\\_/\\_Tantalum\nP 251.9012, 693.4111, -368.0259, 0, 0, 0, 1, Gracho\\_/\\_Galvanite\nP 1096.0237, 137.0296, -224.1894, 0, 0, 0, 1, Aurdred\\_/\\_Periluminum\nP 871.5342, -282.3821, -208.1207, 0, 0, 0, 1, Trathon\\_/\\_Therium\nP 361.5594, 55.2577, -199.0996, 0, 0, 0, 1, Lady\\_Envy\n_You can invis through most of the zone, but there are a few see invis mobs to watch out for._\n_The clockworks hit for a max ~7,000 and are unmezzable and unrootable. They are, however, stunnable. Each of the named drops an item to be turned in later._\n\n---\n\nGive the Counterrotating Flywheel Piston to the Unfinished Subordinate 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nGive the Difference Machine Gearbox to the Unfinished Subordinate 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nGive the Servogizmonic Manipulator to the Unfinished Subordinate 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nGive the Pellucinite Cylinder to the Unfinished Subordinate 0/1 (The Underquarry)\n_Upon handing in:_\nan unfinished subordinate says 'I think, therefore, I am. I am a device of Brell Serilis. I am subordinate to my master Brell. What is happening here? For what purpose am I being used? This is not right. This is not right. I must correct matters, and defend the Underquarry from aggressors. I am very sorry, Lady Envy!'\nYour task 'Scent of a Woman' has been updated.\nLady Envy says 'Kill!! Kill!!'\nLady Envy bites with rusty teeth.\nLady Envy says 'Kill!! Kill!!'\n_Lady Envy attacks you. The clockwork attacks her._\nConvince the Unfinished Subordinate to think for himself 0/1 (The Underquarry)\n_As Lady Envy's health lowers, the clockwork stops._\nLady Envy says, \"I expect ALL of my subordinates, finished or not, to obey my commands! And now, my disobedient clockwork servant, try to function after I remove your primary flange baffle!\"\nLady Envy has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nLady Envy's corpse falls with a soft thump to the ground.\nYour faction standing with Underfoot Autarchs got worse.\nYour faction standing with Underfoot Citizens got better.\nLoot and scrolls with orders or instructions from Lady Envy 0/1 (The Underquarry)\n_Lady Envy drops an item called \"Instructions\"._\nGive Lady Envy's instructions to Peramin Longbottle 0/1 (The Underquarry)\n_Give the item to Peramin at the instance zone-in area to complete the task._\nPeramin Longbottle says 'I can't believe my eyes; a few minutes ago I was prepared to face oblivion, the tearing apart of Underfoot at the steely claws of Lady Envy's clockwork army. Now I am fumbling around for an acceptable way to express my gratitude. Rest as much as you can for I fear the next crisis may be upon us soon. So many disturbances in the Underquarry may awaken Brath from his eternal slumber!'\nYour task 'Scent 